abstract: >-
  Ecoton (Expression Colocalization of Transcripts for Niche Discovery)
  is a computational method for image-based spatial transcriptomics data.
  It takes as input the spatial coordinates and gene identities of individual
  transcripts and outputs a gene-gene colocalization graph along with spatial
  niches defined directly from transcript colocalization patterns.